            <ArticleTitle>[The relation between risk factors and mortality in aortocoronary bypass operations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>184-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Risk factors related to increased mortality were determined on the basis of 329 aortocoronary bypass operations. They were: (1) emergency surgery, (2) poor left ventricular function, (3) reoperation, and (4) pulmonary hypertension. Angina pectoris, recent myocardial infarction, age over 65 years, obesity, significant systemic disturbances, smoking, arterial hypertension, and sex were without effect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
